id: pm-2csj4k
title: Pin tested runtime peers in the published manifest so Bun installs resolve them without peer-range warnings
description: "Bun resolves a bundled package's dependencies from the registry instead of using bundleDependencies. Since @opentelemetry/api 1.10.0 was published on 2026-10-20, bun add and first-run bunx of every pm release print four 'warn: incorrect peer dependency \"@opentelemetry/api@1.10.0\"' lines: @sentry/node 10.76.2 asks for ^1.9.1, Bun picks the newest 1.10.0, and the OpenTelemetry 2.12 packages in the tested closure cap their peer below 1.10.0. Runtime is unaffected because Node resolves the bundled 1.9.1 inside the package, but the install output looks broken and Bun downloads an untested peer set. Measured on 2026-11-01 with fresh caches: 2026.10.31 and 2026.11.1 both print four warnings; repacking 2026.11.1 with the tested peer pinned as a bundled dependency prints none (control: the unmodified repack still prints four). npm, npx and the bundled runtime closure (pm-gh1417) are unchanged. Sentry 11 would drop these OpenTelemetry packages but is blocked separately on pm-t3jxjj."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: agent-ux,bun,dependencies,packaging
created_at: "2026-11-01T05:33:19.084Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-01T06:37:17.027Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-01T06:37:17.004Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-01T06:37:17.004Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: The published manifest pins every non-optional peer target of the runtime ledger to its ledger version and bundles it; Optional-only peers and peers already declared as direct dependencies are left unchanged; The packed-artifact smoke installs the tarball with a plain bun add and fails on any peer-range warning; npm/npx runtime verification and the bundled closure are unchanged
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: low
repro_steps: In an empty project with a fresh BUN_INSTALL_CACHE_DIR run bun add @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.11.1 and read stderr.
resolution: "pinRuntimePeers adds every non-optional peer target of the runtime ledger to the published root manifest at its tested version and bundles it (here @opentelemetry/api 1.9.1, @opentelemetry/core 2.12.0, @opentelemetry/sdk-trace-base 2.12.0); optional-only peers and direct dependencies are unchanged. The packed smoke now runs a plain bun add of the tarball and refuses any peer-range warning, since the existing Bun steps use --silent. RELEASING.md documents the rule."
expected_result: Bun installs of the published package resolve every required peer of the tested closure to its tested version and print no peer-range warnings.
actual_result: "Fresh-cache bun add of the pinned repack prints no peer warnings while the unmodified 2026.11.1 repack prints four; verify-runtime-installation passes for 42 bundled packages; pnpm smoke:npx passes; package-distribution, smoke and artifact-gate specs pass with the pin and the packed-fixture cases fail without it."
affected_version: 2026.11.1
component: packaging
